From: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH 0041] hwmon: macsmc: keep temperature channel numbers stable

macsmc-hwmon registers with HWMON_C_REGISTER_TZ, so a DT thermal zone
names an SMC temperature by channel: thermal-sensors = <&smc_hwmon N>.
Today a temperature node whose key the SMC firmware lacks is skipped and
every later channel moves down by one, so a zone silently binds to the
wrong sensor on a machine (or SMC firmware) that lacks one key. That is
likely on new SoCs whose key set is copied from a sibling board (T6050
J716s uses the J714s key dump).

Keep the slot instead: the channel gets only a label "<node> absent" and
no temp_input, so hwmon's thermal glue skips it and the channel number
stays the index of the node among the temperature-* children.

Base: asahi-wip-7.2 236788cd2 (applies with or without the SMC agent's
0010; the hunks are disjoint).

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>

---
diff --git a/drivers/hwmon/macsmc-hwmon.c b/drivers/hwmon/macsmc-hwmon.c
--- a/drivers/hwmon/macsmc-hwmon.c
+++ b/drivers/hwmon/macsmc-hwmon.c
@@ -647,6 +647,14 @@
 		if (!hwmon->temp.sensors)
 			return -ENOMEM;
 
+		/*
+		 * Temperature channels are thermal zone sensors: a DT
+		 * "thermal-sensors = <&smc_hwmon N>" names channel N, so the
+		 * channel number must be the index of the node among the
+		 * temperature children, whatever this SMC firmware lacks. A
+		 * sensor whose key is missing keeps its slot with only a label
+		 * (no temp_input, so no thermal zone binds to it).
+		 */
 		for_each_child_of_node_with_prefix(hwmon_node, key_node, "temperature-") {
 			sensor = &hwmon->temp.sensors[hwmon->temp.count];
 			if (!macsmc_hwmon_create_sensor(hwmon->dev, hwmon->smc, key_node, sensor)) {
@@ -654,9 +662,16 @@
 
 				if (*sensor->label)
 					sensor->attrs |= HWMON_T_LABEL;
-
-				hwmon->temp.count++;
+			} else {
+				memset(sensor, 0, sizeof(*sensor));
+				scnprintf(sensor->label, sizeof(sensor->label),
+					  "%pOFn absent", key_node);
+				sensor->attrs = HWMON_T_LABEL;
+				dev_info(hwmon->dev, "%pOFn: key not available, channel %d kept empty\n",
+					 key_node, hwmon->temp.count + 1);
 			}
+
+			hwmon->temp.count++;
 		}
 	}
 
